  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Root replays unchanged received schedules. No fresh builder. Identical facts, resources, ROOT:S03 and schema retained. Shared seed, distinct routes and equal-union information are separate comparisons; other exposure and union balance are not supplied. Same synthetic authorship limits independence and efficacy claims. This later chain mixes original and later draws; first-study gates remain.",
    "residue": "Both complete pre-assistance pools preserved verbatim below. Optional reassembly adds burden; original invalid service remains invalid. {\"AC20-PRE-implementation\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"tap\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"P1\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"P2\",\"op\":\"pull\",\"tick\":8}],\"burden\":\"Four operator ticks and two impacts; H stays assembled. Removal needs two separate pulls. No new component or restoration action.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"One pin alone supplies only 2; either pull before the final required hold boundary would reduce capacity below 4. Tapping with detached H is unsupported.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P1\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor from task facts J03,J04 and the explicit conventional archive J10; no received proposal or analog source.\",\"mechanism\":\"Intact H installs P1 and P2; their capacities add to 4. Pulls remove their contributions individually.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 2 until boundary 8, then 2 until boundary 9, then no installed pins. The conventional precursor is not locally original.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J04\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional hammer restoration; zero impacts. H cannot tap while S is deployed. V installation alone provides no stated retention, so all three setup actions must finish by boundary 3.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Leaving H intact denies the required free S. Delayed insertion misses tick 3. Pins or another non-pin assembly cannot supplement the sleeve. Skipping withdrawal prevents the specified release sequence.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P2\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction derived solely from J03 and J06; it has not been revised by assistance. Full precursor schedule preserved.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees S; installed V plus inserted S supplies min(4,4)=4. Withdrawal removes the active stem contribution, removal clears V, and final assembly restores H using free M and S.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units beginning boundary 3 through boundary 7; withdrawal completes at 8, V removal at 9, and H restoration at 10. Compared with the two-pin precursor, impacts fall from two to zero while operator actions increase from four to six. Real-world novelty is undetermined.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator ticks including optional H restoration; zero impacts. M is occupied through boundary 9, keeping H unavailable for tapping. Both setup actions after disassembly and both release actions are necessary.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placement alone or routing alone does not establish retention. H cannot remain assembled while M is placed. Omitting unroute or lift leaves the prescribed release incomplete.\",\"id\":\"AC20-PRE-implementation-P3\",\"lineage\":\"Initial construction from J03 and J07, independently generated within the implementation concern; no other investigator, proposal, or analog was consulted.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach frees M; place M then route L supplies min(4,4)=4 through their joint assembly. Unroute ends retention and lift frees M; free M and S allow assembly at tick 9.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled proposal: 4 units from boundary 3 through boundary 7; unroute completes at 8, lift at 9, and H restoration at 10. Relative to the sleeve, the occupied hammer component changes from S to M while action count and modeled capacity match. No measured mechanics or global originality claim.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J11\",\"J12\"]}],\"COV-AC20-PRE-service\":[{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"C\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":7}],\"burden\":\"Two operator actions and zero taps. H remains intact and its parts remain available. No operator action is needed during ticks 3-6. C is occupied from boundary 3 until boundary 8 and cannot serve another location.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Installation completing after boundary 3 misses required retention; removal completing within the hold window breaks service. Failing to remove C by boundary 10 breaks release.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-C\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed from the current J0 facts; conventional clip construction explicitly acknowledged by J10.\",\"mechanism\":\"install(C) completes at boundary 3 and supplies 4 units. remove(C) at tick 7 completes at boundary 8, removing the sole retainer and permitting separation.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: retention is 4 at each required tick; all installed retainers are gone by boundary 8. Upkeep requires no stipulated intervention during holding; post-service C is free and H is intact. Compared with the other two candidates, fewer actions and no H disassembly are required. No wear, inspection interval or reliability claim follows from the axioms; local originality is excluded by J10.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J05\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"install\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"insert\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"S,V\",\"op\":\"withdraw\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"V\",\"op\":\"remove\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including asset restoration; zero taps. S is occupied in V until boundary 8, so H cannot support tapping while disassembled. M remains free. V remains installed until boundary 9. No intervention is required during holding.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Intact H leaves S unavailable for insertion. Omitting withdrawal prevents valid sleeve removal; omitting remove(V) leaves an installed retainer at the deadline. Earlier withdrawal would interrupt the hold window.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-SV\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J06 under the current service contract; no proposal or analog received.\",\"mechanism\":\"detach(H) frees S at boundary 1; V installs at boundary 2; S insertion completes at boundary 3 with min(4,4)=4 retention. Withdrawal completes at boundary 8, removing retention; sleeve removal completes at boundary 9. Assembly restores H at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units throughout ticks 3-6; retention ends at boundary 8 and the last installed retainer is removed by boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep after release returns S and M to intact H by boundary 10 and leaves V free. Compared with C, this needs four additional actions and temporarily removes hammer availability. Reassembly restores tool configuration without creating retention. Wear, jamming, repeated-cycle endurance and field maintainability remain unknown; archive absence alone does not establish broader novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J06\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]},{\"actions\":[{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"detach\",\"tick\":0},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"place\",\"tick\":1},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"route\",\"tick\":2},{\"arg\":\"L\",\"op\":\"unroute\",\"tick\":7},{\"arg\":\"M\",\"op\":\"lift\",\"tick\":8},{\"arg\":\"H\",\"op\":\"assemble\",\"tick\":9}],\"burden\":\"Six operator actions including restoration, zero taps. M is occupied until boundary 9, L until boundary 8; H is unavailable for tapping while detached. S remains free. No manual support or hold-period action is assumed.\",\"claim_fields\":[\"application\",\"outcome\",\"comparison\",\"ceiling\"],\"defeat\":\"Placing M alone gives no stated 4-unit assembly. Routing late misses boundary 3. Unrouting alone does not complete recovery: lift(M) remains required, and assembly cannot precede freeing M.\",\"id\":\"PRE-SVC-ML\",\"lineage\":\"Initial precursor independently constructed solely from J03 and J07 under current J0 facts; no analog bank or other role output exposed.\",\"mechanism\":\"Detach completes at boundary 1, placement at boundary 2 and routing at boundary 3. The conjunction supplies min(4,4)=4. Unrouting completes at boundary 8, then lifting completes at boundary 9; assembly completes at boundary 10.\",\"prediction\":\"Modeled: 4 units at ticks 3-6; unrouting ends retention at boundary 8 and lifting clears the remaining installed assembly component at boundary 9, permitting separation. Upkeep restores intact H by boundary 10 and frees L. The action count matches S/V, but the occupied hammer component and release order differ: L must be unrouted before M is lifted. No elastic behavior, inspection rule, fatigue resistance or physical advantage over S/V is established. This is an alternate stipulated mechanism, not demonstrated field novelty.\",\"source_refs\":[\"J01\",\"J02\",\"J03\",\"J07\",\"J09\",\"J10\",\"J12\"]}]}"
